###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Training of the water and HEA25 models took about two days on a GeForce
# GTX 1080 Ti (trainingHardware); the small-molecule fits ran on a laptop
# within one or two days. MD speed on one Nvidia A100 (Table V) is recorded
# as inferenceHardware on the CACE T=1 and NequIP water models.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Loss function, optimizer, learning rate and number of epochs are not stated.
# - Energy errors for water are per water molecule (meV/H2O), which has no unit individual: mlips:hasUnit is omitted and the unit is in the label.
# - Table II (ethanol) prints seven energy values for nine columns; the last value of each row is read as CACE (E 2.37 meV, F 7.0 meV/A), consistent with the text. Worth a check against the version of record.
# - Table IV prints energy errors for HEA25 in meV; whether they are per atom is not stated.
# - The reference method is stated only for water (revPBE0-D3); the DFT levels of MD17, 3BPA and HEA25 are not given in this paper, so those data sets carry no reference calculation.
# - For the HEA25 fit the number of radial functions and channels is not stated. The settings of the MACE and N2P2 comparison fits are not stated; the MACE value in Table I (1.9 / 36.2) is quoted from Ref. [18], the model trained here has 1.9 / 46.8.
# - MD stability (ps) and water diffusivity cannot be encoded as metrics.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
